1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:07,500
Welcome to CheetahPay Shield, a privacy-focused merchant payment prototype built for ZECATHON 2026.

2
00:00:07,600 --> 00:00:14,200
CheetahPay explores confidential Web3 checkout and multi-rail settlement, designed natively around the Zcash network.

3
00:00:14,700 --> 00:00:20,500
In the Merchant Invoices suite, merchants create standardized payment requests in ZEC.

4
00:00:20,800 --> 00:00:25,000
When entering an address, CheetahPay analyzes the receiver format.

5
00:00:25,300 --> 00:00:33,800
Unified addresses support shielded receiver pools, while transparent addresses display explicit public ledger warnings.

6
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:41,500
Setting an amount generates a ZIP-321 request with our invoice reference bound directly into the memo field, opening checkout instantly.

7
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:49,500
In Pay with Zcash, customers receive an offline, client-side SVG QR code or can launch their wallet via ZIP-321 protocol dispatch.

8
00:00:49,900 --> 00:00:57,500
It is important to note that generating a payment request formats transaction parameters; it does not broadcast funds.

9
00:00:57,800 --> 00:01:09,000
In our testnet verification terminal, querying on-chain transactions confirms block inclusion, while shielded note plaintext properly remains awaiting external merchant wallet decryption.

10
00:01:09,500 --> 00:01:14,800
For Web2 onboarding, the Fund Wallet interface functions as an illustrative fee calculator.

11
00:01:15,100 --> 00:01:19,200
All calculations and conversion rates are demo estimates, not live quotes.

12
00:01:19,500 --> 00:01:23,500
Live fiat funding is unavailable, and no payment orders or balances are created.

13
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:31,000
Finally, the cross-rail ledger aggregates transaction telemetry with provenance classifications and one-click CSV auditing export.

14
00:01:31,300 --> 00:01:37,000
CheetahPay Shield establishes a practical foundation for privacy-aware commerce on Zcash.
